.TH AVR\-SKILL\-INSTALL 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-skill-install \- Install the avr skill for coding agents.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr skill install
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install the avr skill for coding agents.
.PP
Writes one SKILL.md per location: ~/.claude/skills/avrea-cli for Claude Code (or under CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR) and ~/.agents/skills/avrea-cli for Codex, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Gemini CLI, Devin, OpenCode, Pi and other Agent Skills tools; codex is accepted for agents. Without --agent, both are installed. kiro writes ~/.kiro/skills/avrea-cli for Kiro, which reads only its own folder. Running it again updates the file. A SKILL.md that avr did not install is left alone unless --force is given.
.PP
With --project, the skill goes into .claude/skills and .agents/skills (or .kiro/skills) at the top of the current git repository instead. Commit it so cloud agents working on the repository, such as Devin or Codex cloud, find it. Those environments also need avr installed and AVR_TOKEN set to a personal access token or service token.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr skill install
    avr skill install --agent claude
    avr skill install --project --agent agents
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Location to install for (repeatable): claude; agents for Codex, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini CLI, Devin and others; or kiro. Defaults to claude and agents. (choices: claude, agents, codex, kiro; repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR
Use the current git repository instead of your home directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace a skill that avr did not install.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-skill (1),
.BR avr-skill-show (1),
.BR avr-skill-uninstall (1)
